From e2ec8c5fe83b9744e3905ae2adc114a94044fe1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 14:58:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Count the read cost first for a fourth population, and refute
 it

0110 closed by saying the read cost is the first thing to count and the
only reliable way found to count it is to build the representation for a
candidate population and read boxingSpeculativeReadRequests. This does
that, for the parameter population, and reads the counter before
anything else.

Parameters are the natural fourth candidate: item 3-3 records them as
its one category that cannot reach the numeric tier at all, item 3-8a
deliberately excluded them, 0106 weighted the refusal at 775 877 boxed
writes, and 0107 found their locals the most tree-resident of any cause
at 12.89 free leaf reads per write. That last number is the kind that
has flattered all three previous attempts, which is the reason to count
the cost before believing it.

Counted first: 417 582 speculative-read boxes. The saving is NEGATIVE --
roots consumed by a refused local go 18 657 804 to 18 962 176, 304 372
MORE, because admitting more speculative names makes more trees eligible
through CountSpeculativeLeaves and each mints a root. Corpus 1.003 on
requests and 1.006 on allocations. Refuted, on one measurement, with no
build-then-diagnose cycle.

The per-suite column carries the finding. NavierStokes mints exactly
393 705 speculative-read boxes -- the number this document already
records for item 3-8a's failure, to the digit. On the suite that decides
these items, the fourth population is the third one wearing a different
refusal, and the counter says so before any wall clock was taken.

Also void, and worth stating: 0108 refused PropertyRead, CallResult and
NeverOffered on a consumer-side bound, and 0110 established that bound
was on a different quantity. Those three are un-measured again rather
than eliminated.

The test helper now pins both candidate populations rather than
inheriting them, because three switches into one representation and an
environment variable per switch means a case that reads whatever the
process happens to have is measuring a different engine depending on who
ran it.

8 174 tests with both switches off, and the same 1 293 compiler tests
with both forced on.
